  "live_records": {
    "q-49065": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49065",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{3x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $\\frac{1}{3}$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{3x} & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
