    "q-103593": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103593",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int ({x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the sum rule and get\n\n$$\n\\int ({x}^{3/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, using the power rule in the first term, and taking out the coefficient in the second term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2+1}}{\\frac{3}{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-103593-a",
